---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---
<BaseLayout active="Teaching" title="Teaching">
  <Hero title="Teaching" />
  <section class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Third Level Teaching Experience</h2>
    <div class="teaching-grid">
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>Assistant Professor · 2025–present</h3><p>University of Limerick. Leads modules in design and communication graphics, technology-education pedagogies, and health and safety; develops formative and summative assessment; Course Director and course-board chair for LM095.</p></article>
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>University Teacher · 2023–2025</h3><p>University of Limerick. Led modules in subject pedagogics and health and safety, managed assessment, and continuously developed course modules.</p></article>
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>Teaching Assistant · 2021–2023</h3><p>University of Limerick. Taught design and communication graphics and technology-education pedagogies, managed assessment, represented teaching assistants on the course board, and contributed to module development.</p></article>
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>Second-level teaching</h3><p>St Columba’s Comprehensive School (2020–2021) and Rosses Community School (2019): Engineering, Technology and Graphics, workshop management, computer science/3D-printing support, and TY VEX robotics.</p></article>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:60px">CPD Delivery Experience</h2>
    <div class="teaching-grid">
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>PDST</h3><p>Developed and delivered professional learning in spatial learning with collaborators from Technological University Dublin and the University of Cincinnati, including teacher training at TUS Athlone.</p></article>
      <article class="card teaching-card"><h3>Oide</h3><p>Developed and delivered spatial-learning CPD in Athlone, Dublin and online; supported teachers during implementation and created an asynchronous training site.</p></article>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:60px">Professional learning & certificates</h2>
    <div class="teaching-grid">
      <article class="card certificate"><h3>Developing Spatial Skills initiative</h3><p>PDST confirmation of attendance for development of professional-development days and teaching/learning resources (Aug–Sep 2022).</p></article>
      <article class="card certificate"><h3>Computational Thinking for Every Educator</h3><p>International Society for Technology in Education (ISTE), 15 hours, completed 24 April 2020.</p></article>
      <article class="card certificate"><h3>Research Integrity: Core</h3><p>Oxford University Press / Epigeum, completed 30 December 2021 with an overall score of 87%.</p></article>
      <article class="card certificate"><h3>Inclusion of Learners with Special Educational Needs</h3><p>Hibernia College CPD course, Spring 2021.</p></article>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:60px">Student Evaluation of Teaching</h2>
    <p class="lead">Across the supplied 2021 and 2022 PN4025 evaluations, students rated teaching effectiveness, preparation, enthusiasm, communication, engagement, use of learning technology, and helpfulness very highly.</p>
    <div class="feedback-grid">
      <div class="metric"><span>Effectiveness</span><strong>4.90/5</strong><small>mean of 4.92 & 4.88</small></div>
      <div class="metric"><span>Preparation</span><strong>4.98/5</strong><small>mean of 5.00 & 4.96</small></div>
      <div class="metric"><span>Enthusiasm</span><strong>4.94/5</strong><small>mean of 4.92 & 4.96</small></div>
      <div class="metric"><span>Helpfulness</span><strong>4.92/5</strong><small>mean of 5.00 & 4.83</small></div>
    </div>
    <h3 class="gold" style="margin-top:35px">Anonymized feedback themes</h3>
    <div class="quote-grid">
      <p class="quote">Students repeatedly described explanations as clear, structured and easy to follow, particularly for difficult graphics and SolidWorks concepts.</p>
      <p class="quote">Feedback highlighted approachability, responsiveness and a willingness to provide additional help when students encountered difficulties.</p>
      <p class="quote">Students valued the use of videos, notes, textbooks and online resources, especially when these helped connect 2D graphics with digital modelling.</p>
      <p class="quote">Module-level feedback also identified areas for refinement, including workload, access to suitable computers and a desire for additional worked examples and online drawing-lab support.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Only summarized and anonymized findings are published here; the original SET reports and certificate PDFs are intentionally excluded from the public site.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
